<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25619" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lādon</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάδων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river of Arcadia which flows into the
				Alphēus;</i> the fabled <i>father of
				Daphne</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harenosus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 702</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Q. N. 6, 25, 2</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. E.
				3, 63</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. ad Aen. 3,
			91</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The name of one of Actæon's hounds</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				3, 216</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
